page QueuePage
  Section id:"queue-introduction" py:{ xs:6 md:10 }
    Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:"1fr auto" } gap:5 align:"end"
      Grid columns:1 gap:3
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "SERVER / QUEUE"
        Title size:{ xs:"3xl" md:"6xl" } weight:"black"
          "Queue"
        Text size:"lg" color:"muted"
          "Durable work queues and topic pub/sub with explicit delivery guarantees, authenticated sessions, and one Rust provider contract."
      Button href:"/docs/server" variant:"ghost" scheme:"muted" size:"sm"
        "Server overview"
  Section id:"queue-topology" p:{ xs:5 md:7 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "TOPOLOGY"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Bindings decide where a message goes"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Topics use dot-separated words. A star matches one word and a hash matches zero or more words. Publishing copies a message to every matching queue."
      Code:
        language:"dowe"
        variant:"soft"
        scheme:"surface"
        copyLabel:"Copy commands"
        copiedLabel:"Copied"
        content:"""
          dowe queue init jobs
          dowe queue declare jobs email-workers
          dowe queue declare jobs email-notifications
          dowe queue bind jobs email-workers orders.*
          dowe queue bind jobs email-notifications orders.*
          dowe queue publish jobs orders.created '{"id":"order-42"}'
        """
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:3 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Competing consumers"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Two subscriptions on one queue share deliveries; one active delivery is not duplicated."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Pub/sub copies"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Two queues bound to the same pattern each receive an independent copy."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Durable topology"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Declared queues, bindings, and ready messages persist in the Dowe provider namespace, protected by an exclusive .lock."
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "A live service, second server, and local CLI cannot directly own the same namespace concurrently. Lock acquisition fails closed; use the authenticated service protocol for a namespace owned by a running service."
  Section id:"queue-delivery" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "DELIVERY"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "At-least-once, session-bound decisions"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Each subscription keeps its own streaming session. An opaque receipt can be acknowledged or rejected only once and only on that session."
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:2 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "ACK"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "ACK removes the delivery permanently after the consumer has processed the message."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "NACK"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "NACK with requeue puts the message at the front with redelivered:true; NACK without requeue discards it."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Close and restart"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Closing a subscription or restarting Dowe Queue requeues every persisted delivery still awaiting a decision."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Current guarantee"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Delivery is at-least-once. Exactly-once and visibility timeouts are not part of this release."
  Section id:"queue-providers" p:{ xs:5 md:7 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "PROVIDERS"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "One Rust contract, two transports"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "The provider API and CLI share administration, publication, and subscription semantics without exposing transport details to callers."
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:2 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Dowe"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "The maintained service uses an authenticated WebSocket and durable storage below .dowe/queue. Declare/bind creation, publish destinations, and inspected topology are authoritative."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "RabbitMQ"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "The Rust adapter uses a durable namespaced topic exchange, publisher confirms, and a streaming consumer whose ACK/NACK stays on the same AMQP channel. AMQP reports unknown/None creation, destinations, and topology."
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "Remote Dowe Queue and RabbitMQ connections require TLS. Loopback Dowe connections may use ws://; remote Dowe connections use wss:// with Rustls/WebPKI certificate roots."
  Section id:"queue-service" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "DOWE QUEUE"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Run the maintained service"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "The host is intentionally small: it reserves one authenticated WebSocket path, takes exclusive ownership of each opened namespace, and leaves Queue operations to the shared Rust crate."
      Code:
        language:"dowe"
        variant:"soft"
        scheme:"surface"
        copyLabel:"Copy Dowe"
        copiedLabel:"Copied"
        content:"""
          main
            server port:4150
              queue service
        """
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "Account writers use .dowe/queue/_auth/.lock for exclusive read-modify-write and atomic replacement. A second writer fails closed instead of losing an account record."
      Code:
        language:"dowe"
        variant:"soft"
        scheme:"surface"
        copyLabel:"Copy commands"
        copiedLabel:"Copied"
        content:"""
          dowe queue create-account jobs jobs-api
          dowe dev --target server
          dowe queue inspect jobs
        """
  Section id:"queue-application" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "SERVER-ONLY APPLICATION API"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Publish to an existing queue"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Server actions can select Dowe or RabbitMQ and publish JSON directly to a named queue. The connection, credentials, and payload stay on the server."
      Code:
        language:"dowe"
        variant:"soft"
        scheme:"surface"
        copyLabel:"Copy Dowe"
        copiedLabel:"Copied"
        content:"""
          handler enqueueNotification
            queue appQueue provider:"dowe" host:env.QUEUE_HOST port:env.QUEUE_PORT account:env.QUEUE_USER secret:env.QUEUE_PASSWORD vhost:env.QUEUE_VHOST
            msg sent conn:appQueue.publish queue:"notifications" payload:{ userId:"123" event:"user_created" }
            return json:{ ok:sent.ok messageId:sent.id }
        """
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "Declare QUEUE_HOST, QUEUE_PORT, QUEUE_USER, QUEUE_PASSWORD, and QUEUE_VHOST in the root .env.example with empty or placeholder values. Use ignored .env values for development and .env.live, .env.stage, or .env.uat values for deploys; never expose secrets to Views."
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:2 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Local development"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "dowe dev uses persistent local Dowe storage below .dowe/queue/<vhost> and resolves only vhost. It does not contact the authored provider."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Production providers"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Production resolves provider, host, port, account, secret, and vhost. RabbitMQ uses vhost as its AMQP virtual host and requires TLS outside loopback."
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "msg publish targets a queue that was already declared by the CLI or Rust provider API. It does not declare or bind a queue, reinterpret the name as a topic, or retry after an ambiguous response. The result is exactly { ok, id } and can be returned as shown."
  Section id:"queue-cli" p:{ xs:5 md:7 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "CLI"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Inspect and administer local namespaces"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "The root command calls the same Rust implementation used by runtime and IPC. Direct local commands fail closed when a live service owns the namespace lock."
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:3 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Lifecycle"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Use start, create-account, init, and list for service and namespace setup."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Topology"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Use inspect, declare, and bind to review and change durable topology."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Messages"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Use publish to send JSON and purge to remove only ready messages from one queue."
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "Automatic Dowe client retry is read-only: only inspect may retry. Declare, bind, publish, purge, and ACK/NACK receipt decisions are not retried after an ambiguous response loss because they may already have committed."
  Section id:"queue-boundary" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:4
      Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
        "CURRENT SUPPORT"
      Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
        "Finite publication, streaming consumption"
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "Dowe Source Format supports queue service, server-only Queue connections, and direct msg publish. Source-level consume, subscribe, ACK, and NACK remain streaming Rust provider APIs rather than finite handler statements. Use the Rust provider API for subscriptions and session-bound receipts; secrets, receipts, and payloads remain server-only. RabbitMQ topology management would require a future explicit management authority."
      Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
        "The initial contract also excludes arbitrary AMQP exchange types, priorities, TTL, dead-lettering, exactly-once delivery, visibility timeouts, and transparent subscription reconnection. RabbitMQ integration tests are opt-in and do not require an external broker for the focused suite."
